  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1054 AM CDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\nLingering moisture on the backside of the system will interact\nwith a cold front with a low to medium chance for rain mainly\nacross the northern half of the combined Panhandle Thursday then\nmore of the area Thursday night. Impacts should be minimal.\nHowever, gusty north winds behind the cold front are expected,\nwith strongest gusts perhaps near 40 to 50 mph in the northwest\nzones. This will be the first decent cold front of the year, with\nhighs only in the 60s by Friday, and lows potentially dipping into\nthe 40s and low 50s Thursday night through Sunday night. \n\nWard",
